  data:  # 10d5
    kind: work_item  # 10d5
    title: "backend-agreement renders a nested attribute's carried value as null (is_exported is under supply_chain, not top level) — docs/audits/0019's shape column is wrong"  # 10d5
    status: todo_hard  # 10d5
    priority: 2  # 10d5
    parent:  # 10d5
    tags:  # 10d5
    - adr_0057  # 10d5
    - measurement  # 10d5
    isbefore: []  # 10d5
    duplicate_of: []  # 10d5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 10d5
    pr_ref:  # 10d5
    description: "`hypergumbo backend-agreement` renders a disagreement's CARRIED value with `_shape(node.get(attribute))` (backend_agreement.py, in the per-attribute loop). That reads a TOP-LEVEL key of the serialised node. Nine of the ten merge-pass TRACKED_ATTRIBUTES are top-level in `Symbol.to_dict()`; `is_exported` is NOT — it is nested under `supply_chain` (ir.py ~698, beside tier / is_test_file / …). So `node.get(\"is_exported\")` is None for EVERY node and the shape column prints `null` for a value that exists.\n\nMEASURED: docs/audits/0019 row `is_exported` reads \"`null` ← `false` x41\". Read from the merge pass in memory on the same fixture, the 41 records carry True with alternative False and attribution ('rust',) — the correct rendering is \"`true` ← `false` x41\". The scip-python sample fixture has the same shape column (6 disagreements) and the same error.\n\nSCOPE, stated rather than assumed: only the SHAPE (example values) column is affected. The agree/disagree/one-sided COUNTS come from `attribution` / `alternatives`, which the merge pass writes, and are correct — so no pinned tally in recorded_rust_analyzer_1_94_0.AARDVARK_DNS_ATTRIBUTE_AGREEMENT or recorded_scip_python_0_6_6.SAMPLE_PROJECT_ATTRIBUTE_AGREEMENT moves. WI-dajif's conclusions do not move either.\n\nTHIS IS THE INSTRUMENT FAULT LIVE.md RULE 5 NAMES, and it flattered me: reading `null` as a carried value is what made me file INV-huboz against the merge pass for carrying an absent value over a concrete one. The pass was correct; the reader was not. A wrong instrument exits 0 with a plausible number.\n\nFIX: read the value through a serialisation-aware accessor rather than assuming top level — either resolve the attribute against `to_dict()`'s nesting (a small declared map, or a search of one level of dict-valued keys), or take the carried value from the merge pass's own record instead of re-reading the node. Prefer the latter where available: the instrument already has `attribution`/`alternatives`, and the alternative entries carry their values directly — only the CARRIED side is re-read from the node, which is the asymmetry that caused this.\n\nACCEPTANCE: a unit test on a synthetic artifact whose node carries a nested `is_exported` disagreement renders `true` ← `false`, not `null`; then regenerate docs/audits/0019 with scripts/regenerate-backend-agreement-table (no rust-analyzer needed — it builds from the committed fixture) and confirm the only diff is that shape cell."  # 10d5
    fields: {}  # 10d5
