- op: discuss  # 7a59
  at: '2026-09-19T19:48:34Z'  # 7a59
  by: agent  # 7a59
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7a59
  clock: 3  # 7a59
  nonce: 7a59  # 7a59
  message: "Fixed. The carried value is now read where the attribute actually serialises, and an absence is never rendered as a value.\n\nWHAT CHANGED (`backend_agreement.py`): `_carried(node, attribute)` returns `(found, value)` — the top-level key when there is one, otherwise the attribute inside one of the record's field groups (`supply_chain` is the only one that holds a tracked attribute today). The open payloads — `meta`, `quality`, `attribution`, `alternatives` — are skipped by name: their keys are not field names, so a `meta[\"kind\"]` must never answer a lookup for the record's `kind`. When the attribute is carried nowhere the table prints `(not serialised)`, never `null`: an absence a reader can mistake for a value is precisely how this instrument was wrong.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, on the item's own acceptance:\n1. Synthetic artifact (`test_a_nested_attributes_carried_value_is_read_where_it_serialises`): a merged node with `supply_chain.is_exported = true` and an alternative `false` now measures `shapes == [(\"true\", \"false\", 1)]`. Before the fix the same test measured `[(\"null\", \"false\", 1)]` — red, then green.\n2. Recorded producer input (ADR-0057 §12), the real thing: `test_recorded_fixtures.py::test_the_instrument_reproduces_the_merge_pass` now pins `by_attr[\"is_exported\"].shapes == [(\"true\", \"false\", 41)]` and passes (15 passed). That line pinned `(\"null\", \"false\", 41)` — the defect was committed, pinned and cited.\n3. `scripts/regenerate-backend-agreement-table` → `docs/audits/0019` diff is ONE line, exactly the shape cell: `| is_exported | 107 | 41 | 0 | 0 | null <- false x41 |` becomes `| ... | true <- false x41 |`. No count moved, as the item scoped it.\n4. A second test pins the honesty half: an `attribution` naming an attribute the node carries nowhere renders `(not serialised)`, not `null`.\n\nMUTATION-CHECKED (LIVE.md rule 6 — a control that cannot fail is not a control). Three mutants, each killed with a real `passed|failed` line: restoring the top-level-only lookup (4 failed); returning `(True, None)` instead of `(False, None)` on a miss (1 failed); letting the open payloads answer the lookup (4 failed).\n\nALSO CORRECTED, because the wrong reading was committed in four places and a citation is a claim: `docs/audits/0019`'s hand-written Reading bullet (which blamed the merge pass), ADR-0057 §5's landing note and its WI-dajif tracker-item line, and the comments in both recorded fixtures (`recorded_rust_analyzer_1_94_0.py`, `recorded_scip_python_0_6_6.py`) that described the alternative as beating the incumbent's `None`.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE, still true: the 41 records are a PHANTOM contest — the SCIP arm never assigns `is_exported` and contributes the dataclass default `False`. That is INV-huboz, re-scoped, and the owner has now ruled the cure's shape (the producer declares what it observes).\n\nONE UNRELATED GAP CLOSED: `measure_backend_agreement`'s \"an edge of another language is not this language's\" branch was covered only by the rust-analyzer package's tests, so `hypergumbo-core` did not cover its own module in isolation (99%, line 287). The synthetic artifact now carries a rust-to-rust edge and the core package covers the file 100% on its own."  # 7a59
